# ref-954cf87-stale-tree-rebuild
# Upstream box3d issue #149: stale trees must be rebuilt when the move buffer empties.
# A tiled floor of 25 static unit boxes is created and never moves; one dynamic sphere
# drops onto the middle tile under gravity. The broadphase pair set between the dynamic
# body and the static tiles is what the per-step contact counter observes (a contact
# exists only when its broadphase pair was emitted), so identical contact counts mean
# identical broadphase pair sets. Reference: vanilla float box3d at 954cf87; fixed:
# fixed3d on this branch (the port of step 2, src/broad_phase.c).
# Observable: the per-step contact counter (0 while the sphere falls, 1 once it lands)
#   and the sphere's position, over the full 60 steps.
# Tolerance: twice the measured maximum divergence on this bench against float box3d
#   at 954cf87 (pos 1.26e-3, rot 0, vel 1.74e-3, angvel 0; contact count exact).
#   Values below 8*B3_FIXED_EPSILON are floored to it.
expect pos 0.003 rot 0.0002 vel 0.004 horizon 60 counts exact
world gravity 0 -10 0 dt 1 60 substeps 4 steps 60
body static position -2 -0.5 -2 rotation 0 0 0 1 linvel 0 0 0 angvel 0 0 0
body static position -1 -0.5 -2 rotation 0 0 0 1 linvel 0 0 0 angvel 0 0 0
body static position 0 -0.5 -2 rotation 0 0 0 1 linvel 0 0 0 angvel 0 0 0
body static position 1 -0.5 -2 rotation 0 0 0 1 linvel 0 0 0 angvel 0 0 0
body static position 2 -0.5 -2 rotation 0 0 0 1 linvel 0 0 0 angvel 0 0 0
body static position -2 -0.5 -1 rotation 0 0 0 1 linvel 0 0 0 angvel 0 0 0
body static position -1 -0.5 -1 rotation 0 0 0 1 linvel 0 0 0 angvel 0 0 0
